{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00697",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.5,
      "end_seconds": 13.49,
      "duration_seconds": 11.99,
      "text": "Morning. I'm not here for a lecture. I had COVID in March, and I'm still not right, six months on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.98,
      "end_seconds": 19.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "No lecture. Tell me how you're not right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.31,
      "end_seconds": 33.95,
      "duration_seconds": 11.64,
      "text": "Tired. Not normal tired, flat. I wake up tired. I was running a team of twelve and now I can't concentrate on an email."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.22,
      "end_seconds": 36.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.03,
      "end_seconds": 50.89,
      "duration_seconds": 10.86,
      "text": "Breathless on the stairs, and when I walk quickly. I get a tight feeling in my chest, but no pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.63,
      "end_seconds": 56.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Any chest pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.43,
      "end_seconds": 63.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "No, I said, it's tightness, not pain. No chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.92,
      "end_seconds": 72.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.14,
      "text": "Fair, thank you. What are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.37,
      "end_seconds": 80.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.28,
      "text": "Vitamin D, 1000 units, every day, which I forget about half the time. That's all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.73,
      "end_seconds": 88.25,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "Okay, so the plan is daily, but you often forget. Any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.1,
      "end_seconds": 92.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Type 2 diabetes, diet-controlled."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.6,
      "end_seconds": 99.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Any lung problems in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.97,
      "end_seconds": 105.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "My mum had COPD. She smoked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.39,
      "end_seconds": 109.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "And do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.59,
      "end_seconds": 114.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Never. Not once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.47,
      "end_seconds": 119.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Let me check you. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.95,
      "end_seconds": 123.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Fine. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.63,
      "end_seconds": 146.32,
      "duration_seconds": 8.69,
      "text": "Pulse 82, blood pressure 128 over 80, temperature 36.7, oxygen 97 percent, and weight 79 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.12,
      "end_seconds": 150.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "All right? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.5,
      "end_seconds": 176.75,
      "duration_seconds": 6.25,
      "text": "All fine at rest. Take a deep breath in for me, and out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.37,
      "end_seconds": 182.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "I've been told my chest is clear before. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.94,
      "end_seconds": 189.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "It's clear again today, no wheeze at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.56,
      "end_seconds": 194.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "So what is this? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.43,
      "end_seconds": 216.23,
      "duration_seconds": 18.8,
      "text": "After COVID, many people have fatigue and breathlessness for months. That's what's commonly called long COVID. But I can't rule out asthma coming on after the infection, because of the chest tightness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.63,
      "end_seconds": 221.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Can you do something? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.71,
      "end_seconds": 231.74,
      "duration_seconds": 8.03,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a breathing test, spirometry, to see how your lungs behave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.11,
      "end_seconds": 237.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Right. And treatment? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.22,
      "end_seconds": 253.65,
      "duration_seconds": 14.43,
      "text": "In the meantime, I'm going to give you a salbutamol inhaler, 100 micrograms, two puffs when you're tight or breathless, and we'll see if it helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.32,
      "end_seconds": 257.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Fair. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.1,
      "end_seconds": 268.94,
      "duration_seconds": 8.84,
      "text": "Pace yourself, short breaks during the day, build up activity slowly, and don't push on the bad days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.76,
      "end_seconds": 274.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "That's hard in my job. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.69,
      "end_seconds": 283.02,
      "duration_seconds": 7.33,
      "text": "I know. If your employer allows a phased return, even better. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.41,
      "end_seconds": 288.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "What if it doesn't improve? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.45,
      "end_seconds": 301.83,
      "duration_seconds": 12.38,
      "text": "If your breathlessness is no better in four weeks, come back and see me and we'll look at other tests."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.52,
      "end_seconds": 305.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Right. Thanks. ~"
    }
  ]
}
